  "query_preview": "..\n\nThrough next Friday...\n\nUpper level ridging will work into the region Saturday bringing\nextremely hot temperatures in the triple digits. As shown in the \ntable below, both daily record highs and all time August high \ntemperatures are possible for some climate sites. This airmass \nwill also be extremely dry bringing sub teen relative humidities \nand the potential for some single digit values. 20-25 kt 700 mb \nwinds for locations west of Billings will bring elevated fire \nweather conditions. Due to the combination of hot, dry, and windy \nconditions, a Red Flag Warning has been issued for areas north and\nwest of Billings Saturday.\n\nUpper level ridging begins to flatten out Sunday as a 500 mb\nshortwave trough moves through. This wave will bring a cold front\nthrough Montana Saturday night cooling temperatures 5-10 degrees\nSunday. Ahead of this cold front, a strong 30-40 kt low level jet\nwill impact our eastern zones. This along with poor relative\nhumidity recoveries (30s %) Saturday night will lead to continued\nfire concerns overnight. Dry conditions are expected again Sunday\nwith minimum relative humidity values in the teens for most \nlocations. Continued winds in the 20-30 kt range Sunday will bring\nanother elevated fire weather day. A Fire Weather Watch has been \nissued for most of the region Sunday. \n\nNortherly winds are expected to continue to push in cooler air\nMonday and Tuesday lowering temperatures into the 70s to low 80s\nF. Ensembles are in agreement that flat ridging will return\nWednesday through the end of the week. This pattern likely means\nthe return of temperatures in the 90s F and dry conditions. \n\nBelow is a summary of Saturday forecast highs, with daily and\nAugust records, at each of our main climate stations.\n\nSITE      8/1 FORECAST   8/1 RECORD      AUG RECORD\nBillings     105         102 (2008)    105 (8/2/2024)\nLivingston \t 102 \t\t 101 (2000)    105 (8/5/1961) \nMiles City \t 105 \t\t 104 (2008)    110 (8/7/1995) \nSheridan \t 102\t\t 103 (2008)    106 (8/7/1983) \nBaker\t\t 101 \t\t 99  (2022)    108 (8/12/2018)\n\nLT",
